/*Q21. The Spy Academy maintains information about its operatives using the SpySystem class. Each agent has the following attributes:
• name (String) — The real name of the agent.
• age (int) — The age of the agent.
• codename (String) — The covert codename of the agent.
• isUndercover (boolean) — Indicates whether the agent is currently undercover.
• assignment (String) — The current mission assigned to the agent.
• specialty (String) — The agent's area of expertise.
Class: SpySystem
Implement the SpySystem class to read, process, and display agent information and calculate the average age of all agents.
The class must include the six instance variables listed above to represent an agent's details.
It must also contain the following private static variables:
• totalAgents (int) — stores the total number of agents processed.
• totalAge (int) — stores the sum of the ages of all agents processed.
Implement a static method named displayAverageA ge() that calculates the average age using floating-point division and displays the result
rounded to two decimal places in the format:
Average Age: <average_age>
SpySystem Class Requirements
The SpySystem class must:
1. Read an integer N, representing the number of agents.
2: Read each agent's details in the following order: name, age, codename, undercover status, assignment, and specialty.
3. Display each agent's details immediately after reading them, with each value on a separate line.
4. Update totalAgents and totalAge for every agent processed.
5: After processing all agents, call displayAverageAge() to display the average age.
Input Format:
• The first line contains an integer NV, representing the number of agents.
name
age
codename
isUndercover
assignment
specialty
• The input is repeated for all agents.
Output Format:
For each agent, display the entered details in the same order:
<name>
<age>
<codename>
<isUndercover>
<assignment>
<specialty>
• After displaying the details of all agents, display:
Average Age: <average_age>
• The average age must be calculated using floating-point division and displayed as a double.
Note:
• Round the average age to 2 decimal places.
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class SpySystem {
    String name;
    int age;
    String codename;
    boolean isUndercover;
    String assignment;
    String specialty;
 
    private static int totalAgents = 0;
    private static int totalAge = 0;
 
    SpySystem(String name, int age, String codename, boolean isUndercover,
              String assignment, String specialty) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
        this.codename = codename;
        this.isUndercover = isUndercover;
        this.assignment = assignment;
        this.specialty = specialty;
        totalAgents++;
        totalAge += age;
    }
 
    void display() {
        System.out.println(name);
        System.out.println(age);
        System.out.println(codename);
        System.out.println(isUndercover);
        System.out.println(assignment);
        System.out.println(specialty);
    }
 
    static void displayAverageAge() {
        double avg = totalAgents == 0 ? 0.0 : (double) totalAge / totalAgents;
        System.out.printf("Average Age: %.2f%n", avg);
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            String name = sc.nextLine().trim();
            int age = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
            String code = sc.nextLine().trim();
            boolean under = Boolean.parseBoolean(sc.nextLine().trim());
            String assign = sc.nextLine().trim();
            String spec = sc.nextLine().trim();
            SpySystem agent = new SpySystem(name, age, code, under, assign, spec);
            agent.display();
        }
        displayAverageAge();
        sc.close();
    }
}
